  "description": "A scene depicting a rooster and a hen positioned side by side in an outdoor setting, with text overlaying the image that references a racial stereotype. The rooster is standing upright and facing left, while the hen is positioned slightly behind and to the left, appearing to be in a more subdued posture. The scene is framed by a wooden fence and greenery in the background, with artificial turf underfoot. The text 'chicks be like' is at the top and 'the blacker the berry the sweeter the juice' is at the bottom, creating a juxtaposition between the visual of the chickens and the offensive racial metaphor.",
